WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.600
I'm Eti,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.360
I'm Bori,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.420
I'm George Glover,

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.140
I did the butterfly in the movie,

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.840
the plantain,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.540
I did the caterpillar,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.880
the cow's mouth,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.960
bottom half of the flower,

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.720
I did the top petals,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.720
grass,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.320
cow eyes, chrysalis,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.460
ears of the cow,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.480
what else? Is that it...?

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.480
The stamen! Yeah.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.200
So we've been making this 
film for three days now,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.520
from morning to the evening - in
the basement - in the basement,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.380
having our hands painted.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.560
Doing puppetry, particularly with hands,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.760
I find it quite different from
the other forms of puppetry,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.680
because you're literally
embodying something.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.800
Puppets aren't really thought
of as being scientific,

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.670
even though there are people

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.080
who approach it quite scientifically and
study patterns of movement and things like that.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.120
But I think it's often 
thought of as children's.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:08.520
When Nature first contacted us, 
I think I felt surprised and then

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.440
immediately kind of excited.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.580
I really like it when science and
the arts combine,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.740
because at school I felt like you
either had to choose to go down the

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.520
scientific path or the artistic path. So
when you get options to get a little bit

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.760
more involved with science through
the arts it's really satisfying and

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.360
hopefully vice versa for people from
Nature who are collaborating with us.

